# A skill's shell scripts, and what it copies to the Linux build host (`remote/`), whatever checked them out: with
# CRLF, bash there refuses the first line of a copied script (`set -euo pipefail`). The scripts that copy them also
# strip carriage returns on the way, for a checkout made before this line.
.claude/skills/**/*.sh text eol=lf
.claude/skills/**/remote/** text eol=lf
